.TH SETUP-USER 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
setup-user \- provision a new Linux user with Zsh, SSH keys, and rootless Podman
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo setup-user
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBsetup-user\fR is an administrative utility for Linux servers (systemd-based).
It provisions or updates a user account with the following features:
.IP \(bu 3
Sets the user's login shell to \fB/bin/zsh\fR.
.IP \(bu 3
Adds a specified SSH public key to \fB~/.ssh/authorized_keys\fR with strict permissions (0700/0600).
.IP \(bu 3
Enables systemd user lingering via \fBloginctl enable-linger\fR.
.IP \(bu 3
Configures rootless \fBPodman\fR by starting the user socket (\fBpodman.socket\fR) and enabling the restart service.
.IP \(bu 3
Appends required environment variables (\fBDOCKER_HOST\fR, \fBXDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR, \fBDBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS\fR) idempotently to shell profiles (\fB.bashrc\fR, \fB.zshrc\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Displays brief command-line help and exits.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires root privileges (\fBsudo\fR). Dependencies include \fBbash\fR, \fBsystemd\fR, \fBzsh\fR, and \fBpodman\fR.
